.TH "MANTICORE" "1" "August 25, 2026" "Manticore Search" ""
.SH "NAME"
manticore \- Manticore Search SQL client and lifecycle manager
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBmanticore\fR\ 'u
\fBmanticore\fR [\fICLIENT_OPTIONS\fR]
.HP \w'\fBmanticore\fR\ 'u
\fBmanticore\fR \fBstart\fR [\fBlocal\fR|\fBglobal\fR]
.HP \w'\fBmanticore\fR\ 'u
\fBmanticore\fR \fBstop\fR [\fBlocal\fR|\fBglobal\fR]
.HP \w'\fBmanticore\fR\ 'u
\fBmanticore\fR \fBstatus\fR [\fBlocal\fR|\fBglobal\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBmanticore\fR is the primary user-facing command for querying and managing
Manticore Search. With no lifecycle command it starts the SQL client. When
\fB./manticore_data\fR exists, the command selects that current-directory
local instance; otherwise it selects the normally configured instance.
.PP
An existing local marker is authoritative. A malformed, inaccessible, stale,
or unavailable local instance causes an error rather than an implicit fallback
to the configured instance.
.SH "CLIENT OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Ignore \fB./manticore_data\fR and use exactly this configuration file.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR
Connect directly to a MySQL-protocol listener on HOST. The default host is
\fB127.0.0.1\fR when only \fB--port\fR is specified.
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR
Use PORT for a direct MySQL-protocol connection. The default port is
\fB9306\fR when only \fB--host\fR is specified.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-execute\fR \fISQL\fR
Execute SQL once and exit. Without this option, the client reads interactively
or from standard input.
.TP
\fB\-\-local\fR
Require the current-directory local instance. Do not consult global
configuration.
.TP
\fB\-\-global\fR
Ignore \fB./manticore_data\fR and use normal configuration discovery.
.TP
\fB\-?\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show command help.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the matching Manticore Search build version.
.PP
Direct \fB--host/--port\fR selection is mutually exclusive with
\fB--local\fR, \fB--global\fR, and \fB--config\fR. Direct connections
currently use anonymous MySQL-protocol authentication without TLS.
.SH "LIFECYCLE COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBstart\fR [\fBlocal\fR|\fBglobal\fR]
Start the selected instance and return only after it is ready. \fBstart
local\fR creates the first \fB./manticore_data\fR instance when the directory
is absent.
.TP
\fBstop\fR [\fBlocal\fR|\fBglobal\fR]
Stop the selected instance and wait for shutdown to complete. There is no
separate \fBstopwait\fR command.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR [\fBlocal\fR|\fBglobal\fR]
Report local PID, socket, process, and SQL readiness, or wrap \fBsearchd
--status\fR for the configured instance.
.PP
Without an explicit target, lifecycle commands select local mode when
\fB./manticore_data\fR exists and global mode otherwise. For global lifecycle
operations, an installed and usable \fBmanticore.service\fR is authoritative;
otherwise the matching \fBsearchd\fR executable is invoked directly.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Start a local instance and query it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ manticore start local
$ manticore -e 'SELECT 1 AS value'
$ manticore status
$ manticore stop
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query the configured instance while inside a local project directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ manticore --global -e 'SHOW TABLES'
.fi
.RE

.PP
Connect directly to a Manticore Search MySQL listener:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ manticore -h search.example.com -P 9306
$ manticore -h search.example.com -P 9306 -e 'SHOW TABLES'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read SQL from standard input:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ printf 'SHOW TABLES;\n' | manticore
.fi
.RE
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fB./manticore_data/searchd.sock\fR
Local HTTP Unix socket.
.TP
\fB./manticore_data/searchd.pid\fR
Local daemon PID file.
.TP
\fB./manticore_data/searchd.log\fR
Local daemon log.
.TP
\fB./manticore_data/.history\fR
Local interactive client history.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR searchd (1)
